    "kind": "news",
    "check": "DYJ 8 Jan 1923 p6, read in the block image (DYJ19230108.2.113 area 17): 'PORTSTEWART. There will be no contests. The following were returned:- Messrs. Hugh Lynch, Henry Johnston, Peter Doherty, Saml. Henry, Jas. M'Curdy, Henry O'Neill, Matthew Browne, Andrew M'Gowan, John Tinsley, William Reid, Robert Smyrl, and Daniel Reid.'",
    "url": "https://irishnewsarchive.com/?a=d&d=DYJ19230108.1.6"
  },
  "note": "Election of the Portstewart Urban District Council, January 1923. The Derry Journal reports that there will be no contests, and prints the names of the twelve members returned. The record had 'Robert Sturdy'; the image reads Robert Smyrl (also named as a retiring member in 1925, BNL 7 Jan 1925 p11). Returned unopposed."
